INTERVIEW QUESTIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
"We start by understanding the business requirements and defining standardized KPIs. 
Data comes from multiple source systems such as ERP, CRM, POS, databases and APIs.
We ingest the data into the analytics platform and maintain a raw layer for source traceability. 
The data is then staged, cleaned and transformed using SQL/dbt. 
The transformed data is stored in a cloud data warehouse such as BigQuery and modeled into fact and dimension tables following a star schema.
Business-specific data marts are then created for analytical consumption.
Tableau connects to these curated datasets to build dashboards, and Tableau Server is used to publish, secure, refresh and distribute the dashboards.
Airflow orchestrates the pipeline, while data quality, governance, security, monitoring and lineage are applied across the platform. 
The final objective is to provide trusted insights that help business users make faster and better decisions."











































